From 9de5cc6ecfc163f7a58a0c8fb969381cb4badc61 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AEON-7 <aeon-7@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 21:14:41 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 10/12] [AEON M2] inkling2 gfx12: fused router+sort top-k,
 dot-path MoE for shared experts, MXFP8 hybrid decode, fused combine/norm,
 split-KV merge in attention

- moe_decode: router logits kernel runs a single bitonic-sort top-k for all
  tokens in its last arriver; experts with 3+ rows use a bf16-dequant tl.dot
  path (NVFP4 auto kernel); MXFP8 decode uses per-row GEMV + dot kernel
  (hybrid) and now covers T<=16; expert combine fused into the w2 kernel.
- loop_decode: RMSNorm fused into the up-blend last arriver.
- ops/attention: split-KV partials merged in the attention kernel last
  arriver (AEON_FUSE_SPLIT_COMBINE=0 restores the second launch).
- All last-arriver sites take a workgroup barrier before the arrival atomic
  (fixes a cross-warp visibility race that made identical rows diverge).
- o_proj hook point (HOOKS.oproj) unchanged.

gen_bench bs1 75.8 tok/s, bs8 371.3 tok/s; KL 0.00209 / top-1 98.30% (60 prompts, eager, max-batched 16).
